{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "default_method": "walking",
  "method_notes": "Starting School in Hounslow (Sept 2027 brochure, 'Distance' definition, p.34): for community schools and any own-admission-authority school whose policy uses the LA measuring system, distance is the WALKING route measured by GIS (Synergy/School Admissions Management, Access UK) along OS MasterMap Highways Network road centrelines, from the LLPG/NLPG 'seed point' in the home address footprint, via the nearest network node, to the nearest school gate used by pupils. Equal distances are randomly ordered by the LA database. Community school oversubscription order: looked after, exceptional medical/social need, siblings, children of staff, distance. Academies, free schools and VA faith schools set their own criteria (faith, priority admission areas, Pupil Premium, nearest-school); the brochure refers them to the common definition, so walking is assumed unless stated. Figures are in miles.",
  "method_source": "https://www.hounslow.gov.uk/downloads/file/14354/transferring-to-junior-school-in-hounslow-2027",
